{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following PyPy 3 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original PyPy 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\ndef t(n, h):\n    if dp[n][h] == -1:\n        dp[n][h] = 0\n        for m in range(1, n + 1):\n            left_part = t(m - 1, h - 1) * sum(t(m - 1, i) for i in range(h))\n            right_part = t(n - m, h - 1) * sum(t(n - m, i) for i in range(h - 1))\n            dp[n][h] += left_part + right_part\n    return dp[n][h]\n\n\nn, h = map(int, input().split())\n\n\ndef fill(i, j):\n    if i == 0 and j == 0:\n        return 1\n    elif i == 0 or j == 0:\n        return 0\n    else:\n        return -1\n\n\ndp = [[fill(i, j) for j in range(n + 1)] for i in range(n + 1)]\n\nfor i in range(n + 1):\n    for j in range(n + 1):\n        t(i, j)\n\ntotal = 0\nfor idx in range(h, n + 1):\n    total += dp[n][idx]\nprint(total)\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\nusing namespace std;\n\nlong long t(int n, int h, vector<vector<long long>>& dp) {\n    if (dp[n][h] == -1) {\n        dp[n][h] = 0;\n        for (int m = 1; m <= n; m++) {\n            long long left_part = t(m - 1, h - 1, dp);\n            long long left_sum = 0;\n            for (int i = 0; i < h; i++) {\n                left_sum += t(m - 1, i, dp);\n            }\n            left_part *= left_sum;\n            \n            long long right_part = t(n - m, h - 1, dp);\n            long long right_sum = 0;\n            for (int i = 0; i < h - 1; i++) {\n                right_sum += t(n - m, i, dp);\n            }\n            right_part *= right_sum;\n            \n            dp[n][h] += left_part + right_part;\n        }\n    }\n    return dp[n][h];\n}\n\nlong long fill(int i, int j) {\n    if (i == 0 && j == 0) {\n        return 1;\n    } else if (i == 0 || j == 0) {\n        return 0;\n    } else {\n        return -1;\n    }\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int n, h;\n    cin >> n >> h;\n    \n    vector<vector<long long>> dp(n + 1, vector<long long>(n + 1, -1));\n    \n    for (int i = 0; i <= n; i++) {\n        for (int j = 0; j <= n; j++) {\n            dp[i][j] = fill(i, j);\n        }\n    }\n    \n    for (int i = 0; i <= n; i++) {\n        for (int j = 0; j <= n; j++) {\n            t(i, j, dp);\n        }\n    }\n    \n    long long total = 0;\n    for (int idx = h; idx <= n; idx++) {\n        total += dp[n][idx];\n    }\n    cout << total << endl;\n    \n    return 0;\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00011669908417388797, -2.50339189733495e-06, -7.152555099310121e-07, -2.13382354559144e-05, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -8.535020606359467e-05, -7.152555099310121e-07, -3.576272320060525e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -4.100715523236431e-05, -0.012510748580098152, -0.20145544409751892, -7.510157047363464e-06, -2.0265558760002023e-06, -9.536738616588991e-07, -0.12449152022600174, -3.814689989667386e-06, -0.43368083238601685, -0.07182212173938751, -8.344646857949556e-07, -1.490105023549404e-05, -7.152555099310121e-07, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.00018702188390307128, -0.0011940023396164179, -1.311